## Vendor facts still unverified

- Anthropic’s acceptance of OpenShell’s form-encoded refresh request, actual rotation, replacement-refresh-token persistence, and repeated rotations.
- Stable placeholder resolution and successful supervised Claude requests after each rotation.
- Runtime compatibility of the exact synthetic placeholder while `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` is present. Anthropic’s [authentication precedence](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/authentication) treats that variable as the setup-token credential class, so file shape alone does not prove which credential path Claude selects.
- Host safety and two-gateway isolation using independent grants for each refresh owner. Reusing the host’s current grant is not a valid concurrency proof.
- The cause of the observed `OAuth token revoked` response.
- The remaining live requirements in `rewrite/evidence/A14-t02-live-fixed.md:153-161`, including `jackin-local`, replay, post-shell process state, export, and billing attribution.

The documented 30-day refresh-grant cap still requires periodic interactive reauthorization. None of the hermetic tests justifies flipping T02 from `BlockedVendor`.

No files or credentials were modified or accessed, and no tests were run during this read-only review.